#: manual/verification.md:52
#, fuzzy
msgid "`sample.jsonl` is an old-style record without phases, scales, blocks or a protocol; it checks JSONL parsing, the `dataset_id` fallback of the scaling projection, the stated comparison defaults and the self-contained output. `compare.jsonl` is a hierarchical-design record with a protocol, several confirmatory blocks per scale, an incomplete block and a paired-delta outlier; it checks the comparisons in the HTML and in the printed table. The replay fixture checks artifact parsing, command restoration and the timeout display without executing anything. CI runs the same commands, a coverage budget (`moon coverage analyze`, at most 360 uncovered lines), the interface check (`moon info` with no diff) and `moon fmt --check`."
msgstr "report のフィクスチャは、JSONL の解析、スケーリングの射影、自己完結型の出力を検査します。replay のフィクスチャは、何も実行せずに、アーティファクトの解析、コマンドの復元、タイムアウトの表示を検査します。CI は同じコマンドに加え、カバレッジの予算（`moon coverage analyze`、未カバーの行は最大 360 行）、インターフェースの検査（差分のない `moon info`）、`moon fmt --check` を実行します。"

#: manual/verification.md:64
msgid "Documentation examples"
msgstr "ドキュメントの例"

#: manual/verification.md:66
msgid "Every `moonbit` block in `doc/manual` is a complete test or a top-level definition; blocks that are deliberately partial are fenced `moonbit nocheck`. To check them, put each page's blocks into one temporary package that imports the mare_mark packages it uses (with `moonbitlang/async` for the `async test`s), either under `src/` or in a scratch module joined with the repository in a `moon.work`, and run `moon test` on it. The `cli` pages are tests of the executable package, so their blocks go into a temporary `_test.mbt` file of `src/cli`. Remove the temporary package or file afterwards. The `inspect` contents in the pages are the verified outputs. Outputs that depend on the machine (timings, decisions on real measurements) are never shown."
msgstr "`doc/manual` 内のすべての `moonbit` ブロックは、完全なテストまたはトップレベルの定義です。意図的に部分的なブロックは `moonbit nocheck` でフェンスされています。これらを検査するには、各ページのブロックを、使用する mare_mark のパッケージ（`async test` のために `moonbitlang/async` も）をインポートする 1 つの一時パッケージに入れ、`moon test` を実行します。一時パッケージは `src/` の下に置くか、`moon.work` でリポジトリと結合したスクラッチモジュールに置きます。`cli` のページは実行ファイルパッケージのテストなので、そのブロックは `src/cli` の一時的な `_test.mbt` ファイルに入れます。終わったら一時パッケージやファイルを削除してください。ページ内の `inspect` の内容は検証済みの出力です。マシンに依存する出力（計時値、実際の計測に基づく判断）は決して示しません。"

#: manual/verification.md:78
msgid "The catalogs and attachments are checked with the Luna-Flow `lunadoc` tool: `lunadoc check --compile` (links, catalogs, Typst attachments) and `lunadoc status` (translation coverage)."
msgstr "カタログと添付資料は Luna-Flow の `lunadoc` ツールで検査します。`lunadoc check --compile`（リンク、カタログ、Typst の添付資料）と `lunadoc status`（翻訳のカバレッジ）です。"

#: manual/verification.md:82
msgid "What the tests prove, and what they do not"
msgstr "テストが証明すること、しないこと"

#: manual/verification.md:84
msgid "`stats`: robust summaries, decision thresholds, invalid-input errors, and that bootstrap intervals are deterministic and lie within the range of the deltas, the decision for ties and for thresholds that are `0`, `NaN`, infinite or negative, and `NaN` propagation through `summarize` and `compare_paired`. Not: coverage of the intervals (the design page computes it for small samples), BCa or hierarchical resampling."
msgstr "`stats`: 頑健な要約、判断の閾値、不正な入力に対するエラー、ブートストラップ区間が決定的で差の範囲内に収まること、同値および `0`・`NaN`・無限大・負の閾値に対する判断、そして `summarize` と `compare_paired` での `NaN` の伝播。証明しないこと: 区間の被覆確率（小標本については設計ページで計算しています）、BCa や階層的な再標本化。"

#: manual/verification.md:90
#, fuzzy
msgid "`model` and `event`: that every protocol field changes the identity, the published FNV-1a test vectors, run-id escaping, and that the `protocol` object round-trips through JSON text for every variant and edge value. Not: freedom from 64-bit digest collisions."
msgstr "`model` and `event`: that every protocol field changes the identity, the published FNV-1a test vectors, run-id escaping, and that the `protocol` object round-trips through JSON text for every variant and edge value. Not: freedom from 64-bit digest collisions."

#: manual/verification.md:94
#, fuzzy
msgid "`runner`: validation before timing, timing boundaries per setup policy (synchronization, reset exclusion), calibration bounds, balanced order, the dataset and event sequence of each experiment design (snapshots of the fixed design, unique dataset ids, the block-to-dataset mapping), each validation coverage, the `repeats_per_dataset` rules, the rejection of `PerRun` setup with several datasets, worker abort and timeout, minimized replayable failures, relational mismatches, outcome counting. Not: the quality of a machine's timer or the absence of interference from other processes."
msgstr "`runner`: 計時の前の検証、セットアップポリシーごとの計時の境界（同期、リセットの除外）、キャリブレーションの上下限、バランスの取れた順序、ワーカーの異常終了とタイムアウト、最小化されたリプレイ可能な失敗、関係による不一致、結果の集計。証明しないこと: マシンのタイマーの品質や、他のプロセスによる干渉がないこと。"

#: manual/verification.md:103
#, fuzzy
msgid "`env_detect`: the target and GC labels, the timestamp and run-id formats (including leap days and the `seq<n>` fallback), that overrides win and that a field is undetected exactly when it holds its fallback, the `/proc/cpuinfo` parser and the subprocess wrapper on native. Not: that a particular host's probes succeed."
msgstr "`env_detect`: the target and GC labels, the timestamp and run-id formats (including leap days and the `seq<n>` fallback), that overrides win and that a field is undetected exactly when it holds its fallback, the `/proc/cpuinfo` parser and the subprocess wrapper on native. Not: that a particular host's probes succeed."

#: manual/verification.md:108
#, fuzzy
msgid "`report`: projection rules (confirmatory only, medians per scale, linear and categorical axes, the `dataset_id` fallback), pairing by block, incomplete and outlier counts, the outlier policy on paired deltas, the recorded and default settings, row seeds, decisions and reasons of every `Unknown` and `Invalid` case, escaping, version gating, self-contained output. Not: rendering in a particular browser, or the coverage of the intervals."
msgstr "`report`: projection rules (confirmatory only, medians per scale, linear and categorical axes, the `dataset_id` fallback), pairing by block, incomplete and outlier counts, the outlier policy on paired deltas, the recorded and default settings, row seeds, decisions and reasons of every `Unknown` and `Invalid` case, escaping, version gating, self-contained output. Not: rendering in a particular browser, or the coverage of the intervals."

#: manual/verification.md:115
msgid "`tune` and `tune_gemm`: median scoring, order-independent selection, Pareto filtering, candidate constraints, bitwise agreement of blocked and reference GEMM over all layouts with tails. Not: that a tuned candidate is fastest on another CPU. `seeded_order` is tested for spreading ids that differ only at the end, not for statistical randomness."
msgstr "`tune` と `tune_gemm`: 中央値によるスコア付け、順序に依存しない選択、パレートのフィルタリング、候補の制約、端数を含むすべてのレイアウトにおけるブロック化 GEMM と参照 GEMM のビット単位の一致。証明しないこと: チューニングした候補が別の CPU でも最速であること。`seeded_order` については末尾だけが異なる ID を散らばらせることをテストしており、統計的なランダム性はテストしていません。"

#: manual/verification.md:120
